WEBVTT

00:00:33.303 --> 00:00:34.583
Hey,  Maddie.

00:00:34.586 --> 00:00:37.077
Listen, I, uh, hate to pull you away,

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:39.769
But I'm gonna need you to come
back to the office with me.

00:00:39.807 --> 00:00:41.376
Really?

00:00:41.379 --> 00:00:45.284
Yeah, it turns out I got to
file those docs by midnight.

00:00:45.287 --> 00:00:48.841
I'm gonna need you to, um...

00:00:51.289 --> 00:00:53.260
This isn't working at all, is it?

00:00:53.263 --> 00:00:54.733
No, it's not, Nate.

00:00:54.736 --> 00:00:55.905
Listen, I've had a couple.

00:00:56.109 --> 00:00:57.789
I shouldn't really drive.

00:00:58.093 --> 00:01:00.825
Could you just give me a lift
--  I already called you a cab.

00:01:02.452 --> 00:01:04.212
I'll see you in the morning.

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:13.270
Does that happen a lot?

00:01:13.273 --> 00:01:15.585
Only on the days that end with a Y.

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:27.348
You okay?

00:01:28.594 --> 00:01:29.573
Yeah.

00:01:33.323 --> 00:01:34.623
I've got to go.

00:03:31.599 --> 00:03:33.320
Here is the detective

00:03:40.236 --> 00:03:41.556
That's a pretty nasty bite.

00:03:42.361 --> 00:03:43.470
You know what bit him?

00:03:43.473 --> 00:03:46.185
I haven't quite
determined that just yet.

00:03:47.671 --> 00:03:48.680
Come on, doc.

00:03:48.683 --> 00:03:50.083
Off the record.

00:03:50.898 --> 00:03:54.261
Okay, way, way off the record.

00:03:54.856 --> 00:03:58.380
If I didn't know better, I'd say
the guy was attacked by a wolf.

00:03:58.383 --> 00:04:02.167
But unless I know that the zoo is missing
one of their lobos, I'm going with pit bull.

00:04:02.170 --> 00:04:03.841
I like my job.

00:04:03.844 --> 00:04:05.033
Yeah, I hear you.

00:04:05.036 --> 00:04:06.035
One more thing.

00:04:06.038 --> 00:04:08.841
This guy -Was his heart missing?

00:04:09.956 --> 00:04:11.175
Yeah, how did you know that?

00:04:11.178 --> 00:04:12.708
I haven't even finished my report.

00:04:12.711 --> 00:04:14.231
Lucky guess.

00:04:18.583 --> 00:04:21.105
This lawyer guy first
heart-Free corpse in town?

00:04:21.108 --> 00:04:22.368
First man.

00:04:22.641 --> 00:04:24.802
Over the past year, several
women have gone missing.

00:04:25.527 --> 00:04:30.213
Dead bodies all washed up later in the bay,
too deteriorated to draw firm conclusions.

00:04:30.216 --> 00:04:32.468
But no hearts. No hearts

00:04:32.511 --> 00:04:34.231
They were all hookers
working at hunter's point.

00:04:34.234 --> 00:04:36.030
Cops are trying to
keep things under wrap,

00:04:36.033 --> 00:04:39.652
But they're looking for a serial
killer. And the lunar cycle?

00:04:39.655 --> 00:04:43.059
Yeah, month after month, all the murders
happened in the week leading up to the full moon.

00:04:43.062 --> 00:04:45.333
Which is this week. There is the lawer

00:04:45.336 --> 00:04:46.586
Awesome.

00:04:47.942 --> 00:04:50.133
Dean, could you be a
bigger geek about this?

00:04:50.136 --> 00:04:52.381
I'm sorry, man, but what
about a human by day,

00:04:52.384 --> 00:04:55.426
A freak animal killing machine
by moonlight don't you understand?

00:04:55.429 --> 00:04:59.078
We haven't seen one since we were kids.

00:04:59.304 --> 00:05:00.574
Okay, sparky.

00:05:00.887 --> 00:05:01.876
Then you know what?

00:05:01.879 --> 00:05:05.018
After we kill it, we can go to disneyland.
Know what the best part about it is?

00:05:05.021 --> 00:05:09.149
We already know how to
bring these suckers down.

00:05:09.845 --> 00:05:11.055
So what's our next move?

00:05:11.058 --> 00:05:12.908
Talk to the girl who found the body.

00:05:14.685 --> 00:05:15.704
Madison: I don't understand.

00:05:15.707 --> 00:05:17.147
I already gave my statement to you.

00:05:17.150 --> 00:05:19.632
Well, we just need to
verify a few things.

00:05:19.635 --> 00:05:22.838
This is my neighbor glenn.
Glenn, this is detective...

00:05:22.841 --> 00:05:25.129
Landis. And detective dante.

00:05:25.167 --> 00:05:27.307
Well, guess I'll leave you to it.

00:05:30.140 --> 00:05:30.855
Okay.

00:05:30.858 --> 00:05:32.317
Thanks for the casserole.

00:05:33.392 --> 00:05:34.562
Oh, how thoughtful.

00:05:35.036 --> 00:05:36.756
Just call if you need anything.

00:05:39.394 --> 00:05:40.273
He's sweet.

00:05:40.276 --> 00:05:42.177
He came over to check on me.

00:05:42.701 --> 00:05:44.431
Have a seat.

00:05:50.166 --> 00:05:51.906
You must be pretty shaken up.

00:05:52.591 --> 00:05:54.582
You were nate mulligan's
assistant, right?

00:05:54.585 --> 00:05:55.584
For two years, yeah.

00:05:55.587 --> 00:05:57.277
So you knew all about him.

00:05:57.280 --> 00:05:59.572
Probably knew more
about him than he did.

00:05:59.575 --> 00:06:00.584
Nate was...

00:06:00.947 --> 00:06:02.197
He was nice.

00:06:03.332 --> 00:06:05.584
But...

00:06:05.587 --> 00:06:09.014
You get a few scotches in him, and he
started hitting on anyone in a 5-Miles radius.

00:06:09.017 --> 00:06:10.964
You know the type.

00:06:14.645 --> 00:06:17.387
Yeah. I do, actually.

00:06:18.061 --> 00:06:20.694
Did, uh, did he have any
enemies? What do you mean?

00:06:20.697 --> 00:06:22.494
Sure looked like an animal attack.

00:06:22.497 --> 00:06:24.752
We're just covering all the bases.

00:06:24.755 --> 00:06:25.977
Anyone that might have
had a beef with him

00:06:25.980 --> 00:06:28.731
Former client, an ex. What?

00:06:28.734 --> 00:06:30.391
Well, this is embarrassing,

00:06:30.394 --> 00:06:32.123
But my ex-Boyfriend, kurt.

00:06:32.126 --> 00:06:33.693
Kurt have a last name? Mueller

00:06:33.731 --> 00:06:35.644
After we broke up, he went kind of nuts.

00:06:35.647 --> 00:06:36.806
He's...

00:06:37.150 --> 00:06:39.231
Well, he's kind of been stalking me.

00:06:39.234 --> 00:06:42.447
He got it in his head that something
was going on between Nate and I.

00:06:42.450 --> 00:06:44.040
He showed up at my office.

00:06:44.043 --> 00:06:45.861
And what happened? Kurt
got into it with nate.

00:06:45.864 --> 00:06:48.839
Threw a punch before security grabbed
him. I was lucky to keep my job.

00:06:48.842 --> 00:06:50.102
When was the last time you saw kurt?

00:06:50.105 --> 00:06:51.205
A few nights ago.

00:06:51.208 --> 00:06:52.878
Actually, the night Nate died.

00:06:52.881 --> 00:06:55.674
We were all grabbing drinks at
this bar, and Kurt showed up.

00:06:55.677 --> 00:06:56.515
And?

00:06:56.518 --> 00:06:57.437
Nothing.

00:06:58.041 --> 00:06:59.040
It was...

00:06:59.043 --> 00:07:01.084
Like he was watching me.

00:07:01.087 --> 00:07:02.577
Then he was gone.

00:07:02.580 --> 00:07:04.010
Tell you the truth...

00:07:04.705 --> 00:07:06.375
He scares me.

00:07:08.963 --> 00:07:10.142
So, what do you think?

00:07:10.145 --> 00:07:12.227
Stalker ex-Boyfriend.

00:07:12.230 --> 00:07:13.469
He hates the boss.

00:07:13.472 --> 00:07:14.722
And he was there that night.

00:07:14.725 --> 00:07:16.124
Think he's our dog-Faced boy?

00:07:16.388 --> 00:07:18.269
Well, it's a theory.

00:07:19.023 --> 00:07:20.223
We've had worse.

00:07:20.847 --> 00:07:23.399
What do you say we pay kurt a visit?

00:08:49.123 --> 00:08:51.595
Nothing but leftovers and a six-Pack.

00:08:52.079 --> 00:08:53.308
Check the freezer.

00:08:53.311 --> 00:08:56.695
Maybe there's some human hearts
behind the haagen-Dazs or something.

00:09:22.971 --> 00:09:24.200
Sam, come here.

00:09:29.704 --> 00:09:31.044
Check it out.

00:09:42.750 --> 00:09:44.080
Somebody there?

00:10:15.395 --> 00:10:17.186
I'll call 911.

00:10:24.874 --> 00:10:27.597
I'd say Kurt's looking
more and more like our cujo.

00:10:27.600 --> 00:10:30.562
If he's out here, we
better check on Madison.

00:10:35.315 --> 00:10:36.334
What's going on?

00:10:36.337 --> 00:10:38.358
Police business, glenn.

00:10:40.305 --> 00:10:41.524
What is it?

00:10:43.411 --> 00:10:45.933
Well, maybe we should talk privately?

00:10:46.557 --> 00:10:48.128
Has kurt been here?

00:10:48.131 --> 00:10:49.871
Not exactly.

00:10:50.315 --> 00:10:52.957
What exactly does "not exactly" mean?

00:10:52.960 --> 00:10:57.256
Well, he was outside
last night -Just looking.

00:10:57.259 --> 00:10:59.500
Just looking at me.

00:10:59.884 --> 00:11:01.584
Has he done something?

00:11:01.587 --> 00:11:04.240
We're not really sure.
It's probably nothing.

00:11:04.243 --> 00:11:05.322
But...

00:11:05.325 --> 00:11:06.665
We just don't want to take any chances.

00:11:06.668 --> 00:11:08.841
In fact, one of us should
probably stay here with you,

00:11:08.844 --> 00:11:10.574
Just in case he stops by.

00:11:10.856 --> 00:11:13.208
Where does he work? He owns a body shop.

00:11:13.344 --> 00:11:16.133
You mind grabbing that
address for us? Thanks.

00:11:17.990 --> 00:11:21.033
All right, you go.I'll stay.
You go after the creepy ex.

00:11:21.036 --> 00:11:22.336
I'm gonna hang here with the hot chick.

00:11:22.339 --> 00:11:24.570
Why do you always get to
hang out with the girls?

00:11:24.573 --> 00:11:26.003
Because I'm older.

00:11:26.577 --> 00:11:29.570
No, screw that. We settle
this the old-Fashioned way.

00:11:35.896 --> 00:11:37.757
Dean, always with the scissors.

00:11:37.760 --> 00:11:40.191
Shut up. Shut up. Two out of three.

00:11:44.233 --> 00:11:44.633
God!

00:11:44.734 --> 00:11:46.424
Bundle up out there, all right?

00:12:08.260 --> 00:12:11.063
Um, do you want to sit on the
couch? No. No, no, I'm okay.

00:12:11.066 --> 00:12:13.829
It's more comfortable. Uh, I'm fine.

00:12:34.353 --> 00:12:37.045
You know, I think I
will sit on the couch.

00:12:50.795 --> 00:12:52.215
Let me guess.

00:12:52.218 --> 00:12:55.209
You're sitting on her couch trying
to think of something to say.

00:12:55.212 --> 00:12:56.941
Did you find kurt? He
hasn't been at work all week,

00:12:56.944 --> 00:13:00.153
But because I'm good, and
I mean really, really good,

00:13:00.156 --> 00:13:02.977
I got a line on where he might be.

00:13:04.904 --> 00:13:07.606
What's she wearing? Bye, dean.

00:13:10.635 --> 00:13:12.385
Oh, sammy.

00:13:23.070 --> 00:13:25.892
Who died and made you sheriff?
I will call who I want.

00:13:26.096 --> 00:13:29.640
Whatever you want. Look what time it is.

00:13:29.643 --> 00:13:32.536
You're gonna wake her up and start talking about
- I saw that.

00:13:32.539 --> 00:13:34.409
What? Saw what?

00:13:34.653 --> 00:13:35.989
Okay, this
is the deal --

00:13:35.992 --> 00:13:39.299
My house, my tv.

00:13:39.302 --> 00:13:41.461
I never get to watch my show,

00:13:41.464 --> 00:13:43.302
So suck it up.

00:13:55.745 --> 00:13:56.699
Wait, so

00:13:56.702 --> 00:14:00.936
So kindall married ethan's
father just to get back at him?

00:14:01.567 --> 00:14:04.479
And now she's set to inherit all the
casinos that were supposed to go to ethan.

00:14:04.482 --> 00:14:06.854
What a bitch!

00:14:09.442 --> 00:14:12.225
Admit it -You're hooked.
No, no, no, no, no, no.

00:14:12.228 --> 00:14:14.740
I wouldn't say I'm hooked.

00:14:17.969 --> 00:14:19.690
Can I ask you a question?

00:14:19.933 --> 00:14:22.906
It's ... it's a little personal.

00:14:22.909 --> 00:14:25.211
You've seen my entire
underwear collection.

00:14:25.214 --> 00:14:27.515
Go ahead.

00:14:27.518 --> 00:14:29.299
Okay, um...

00:14:29.923 --> 00:14:32.936
Well, you're -You're clearly smart.

00:14:32.939 --> 00:14:35.872
I mean, your house is full
of great books, you know?

00:14:35.875 --> 00:14:39.279
And you're independent. Uh-Huh.

00:14:40.274 --> 00:14:43.317
What were you doing with kurt?

00:14:44.863 --> 00:14:46.704
I don't know.

00:14:47.659 --> 00:14:49.624
I mean, it's not like he
introduced himself, like,

00:14:49.627 --> 00:14:52.398
Hi, I'm possessive and controlling,
and I like to punch people.

00:14:52.401 --> 00:14:55.180
Want to be my girlfriend?

00:14:55.183 --> 00:14:56.421
Yeah, well,

00:14:56.424 --> 00:14:58.201
I guess we all make mistakes.

00:14:58.204 --> 00:15:00.892
Yeah, well, mine's wanted by the police.

00:15:01.536 --> 00:15:04.630
You want to know why I
stayed with him? Really?

00:15:06.256 --> 00:15:08.297
I was too insecure to leave.

00:15:08.300 --> 00:15:11.654
Well, I find that hard to believe.
You don't really seem like the type.

00:15:11.657 --> 00:15:13.818
Yeah, well some stuff happened.

00:15:14.252 --> 00:15:16.794
My life changed, I changed,
for the better, I think.

00:15:16.797 --> 00:15:20.120
What happened? Well, for
one thing, I got mugged.

00:15:21.055 --> 00:15:23.046
And that's supposed to be a good thing?

00:15:23.049 --> 00:15:24.755
I know, it sounds strange,

00:15:24.758 --> 00:15:26.218
And don't get me
wrong -It rattled me --

00:15:26.221 --> 00:15:28.451
But then it hit me.

00:15:28.454 --> 00:15:33.517
I could keep feeling sorry for myself
or I could take control of my life.

00:15:33.520 --> 00:15:35.631
I chose the latter.

00:15:36.286 --> 00:15:38.207
First thing I did was
tell kurt he had to go.

00:15:38.210 --> 00:15:41.493
Smart move. Apparently.

00:15:41.496 --> 00:15:44.479
Everything else just
opened up, blossomed.

00:15:44.743 --> 00:15:46.643
It's all been wonderful, really.

00:15:47.418 --> 00:15:48.808
What?

00:15:50.634 --> 00:15:52.810
Doesn't everybody think that being
a victim of random violence is

00:15:52.813 --> 00:15:54.938
The best thing that
ever happened to them?

00:15:54.963 --> 00:15:57.024
Yeah, not so much.

00:16:00.454 --> 00:16:02.355
You're...

00:16:02.358 --> 00:16:04.088
Unusual.

00:16:05.724 --> 00:16:07.735
Unusual like...

00:16:08.109 --> 00:16:10.661
"Unusual"? No, no, no.

00:16:10.664 --> 00:16:13.597
Unusual like...

00:16:16.416 --> 00:16:18.206
Impressive.

00:16:22.007 --> 00:16:23.327
You think so?

00:16:28.300 --> 00:16:29.669
Sorry.

00:16:32.999 --> 00:16:34.899
Hey. I found him.

00:16:34.953 --> 00:16:37.214
Good. Don't take your eyes off him.

00:16:40.905 --> 00:16:42.785
Oh, yeah, my eyes are glued.

00:16:42.788 --> 00:16:44.769
Look, sammy, I got to let you go.

00:16:44.772 --> 00:16:47.385
I, uh, I don't want to miss anything.

00:16:57.788 --> 00:16:59.379
So, um...

00:17:00.083 --> 00:17:01.493
I'm gonna turn in.

00:17:01.496 --> 00:17:02.455
Okay, yeah.

00:17:02.458 --> 00:17:04.719
Well, I'll be here. Okay.

00:17:04.722 --> 00:17:09.869
If you hear anything, if you
wake up, just -Just call out.

00:17:12.618 --> 00:17:15.401
Okay. Okay.

00:18:47.578 --> 00:18:50.631
Dean, you okay? Yeah,
now that I'm conscious.

00:18:50.634 --> 00:18:52.494
The werewolf knocked me out.

00:18:52.497 --> 00:18:53.987
Sam, it's madison.

00:18:53.990 --> 00:18:55.079
What? !

00:18:55.082 --> 00:18:57.635
Yeah, awesome job of
keeping an eye on her.

00:19:02.056 --> 00:19:04.889
Dean, I've been here the whole
time. She's in bed asleep.

00:19:04.892 --> 00:19:06.212
Well, she wasn't an hour ago.

00:19:06.215 --> 00:19:09.809
Check her right arm. I nicked
her with a silver knife.

00:19:12.197 --> 00:19:13.576
Morning.

00:19:20.944 --> 00:19:23.456
Um, wherare my pajamas?

00:19:26.345 --> 00:19:27.995
Sam?

00:19:27.998 --> 00:19:30.019
What's going on?

00:19:32.026 --> 00:19:34.147
Where are you going?

00:19:34.150 --> 00:19:36.172
I'm not going anywhere.

00:19:36.175 --> 00:19:38.626
And neither are you.

00:19:45.253 --> 00:19:46.542
You're psychotic.

00:19:46.545 --> 00:19:49.458
The whole "I'm a cop"
trick. God, I am so stupid.

00:19:49.461 --> 00:19:51.793
Well, I guess neither of us
are who we said we were, huh?

00:19:51.796 --> 00:19:53.256
Sam, you're sick, okay?

00:19:53.259 --> 00:19:54.658
You're imagining things.

00:19:54.661 --> 00:19:57.193
Monsters don't exist. Not really.

00:19:57.196 --> 00:19:59.568
You know what? Save the act.

00:19:59.571 --> 00:20:01.512
It's not an act!

00:20:01.515 --> 00:20:05.149
I am not a werewolf!
There is no such thing!

00:20:05.152 --> 00:20:07.564
It's made up, all right?

00:20:07.567 --> 00:20:09.779
They're not real! You
know they're not real!

00:20:09.782 --> 00:20:11.642
No? Then where did that come from?

00:20:11.645 --> 00:20:13.015
I don't know!

00:20:13.429 --> 00:20:16.051
Sam, god, you need help.

00:20:16.665 --> 00:20:19.107
Please, don't do something
that you're gonna regret.

00:20:19.110 --> 00:20:21.803
I'm not what you think I am.

00:20:21.806 --> 00:20:23.526
I'm not.

00:20:35.743 --> 00:20:37.484
How you doing?

00:20:38.759 --> 00:20:41.131
My head feels great, thanks.

00:20:41.946 --> 00:20:43.556
We got to talk.

00:20:49.521 --> 00:20:51.602
She says she has no idea
what I'm talking about.

00:20:51.605 --> 00:20:52.754
She's lying.

00:20:53.188 --> 00:20:54.865
Maybe. Or maybe she really
doesn't know she's changing.

00:20:54.868 --> 00:20:57.804
Maybe when the creature
takes over, she blacks out.

00:20:57.807 --> 00:20:59.698
Like a really hot incredible hulk?

00:20:59.701 --> 00:21:03.025
Dude, she ganked her boss and her ex-Boyfriend.
That doesn't sound ration unconscious.

00:21:03.028 --> 00:21:04.578
But what if it was, dean?

00:21:04.581 --> 00:21:08.005
What if some animal part of her
brain saw both those guys as threats?

00:21:08.008 --> 00:21:10.430
Hell, the cop, too. Are
you the dog whisperer now?

00:21:10.433 --> 00:21:12.263
Look, man, I just...

00:21:13.308 --> 00:21:15.662
I don't know. There was
something in her eyes.

00:21:15.665 --> 00:21:16.699
Yeah, she's killing people.

00:21:16.702 --> 00:21:19.280
But if she has no control..
Exactly she can't control it.

00:21:19.284 --> 00:21:21.280
Even if she's telling the truth,
it's not gonna change anything.

00:21:21.283 --> 00:21:23.704
I'm not putting a bullet through some
girl who has no idea what's happening.

00:21:23.707 --> 00:21:25.277
Sam she is master You're
feeling sorry for her?

00:21:25.280 --> 00:21:27.143
Maybe I understand her.

00:21:29.240 --> 00:21:33.716
Look, there might be another way we can get
the job done without having to waste her.

00:21:38.679 --> 00:21:40.961
Are you thinking what
I think you're thinking?

00:21:41.705 --> 00:21:42.935
Dad's theory.

00:21:42.938 --> 00:21:47.223
Lycanthropy might have a cure if you kill the
werewolf who bit you, severing the bloodline.

00:21:47.226 --> 00:21:49.247
Might have a cure. Meaning who knows?

00:21:49.250 --> 00:21:51.552
It's worth a shot.  We don't
even know where to look.

00:21:52.016 --> 00:21:55.460
The puppy that bit her -- It could be
anyone, anywhere. Could have been years ago.

00:21:57.717 --> 00:21:59.648
No, I don't think so.

00:22:06.505 --> 00:22:07.564
Madison...

00:22:07.907 --> 00:22:09.818
When were you mugged?

00:22:11.505 --> 00:22:13.435
Please, it's important, all right?

00:22:13.438 --> 00:22:14.878
Just answer the question.

00:22:18.829 --> 00:22:20.810
About a month ago.

00:22:20.813 --> 00:22:22.644
Did you see the guy? No.

00:22:22.647 --> 00:22:23.996
He grabbed me from behind.

00:22:24.000 --> 00:22:25.580
Did he bite you?

00:22:29.751 --> 00:22:31.642
How did you know that?

00:22:32.757 --> 00:22:34.057
Where?

00:22:34.060 --> 00:22:36.171
O-On the back of my neck.

00:22:46.234 --> 00:22:47.774
Oh, that's just a love bite.

00:22:47.777 --> 00:22:50.279
Believe me, that could
have been a lot worse.

00:22:50.923 --> 00:22:54.127
Where were you at the time?
Walking home from a friend's loft.

00:22:54.130 --> 00:22:55.069
Let me guess.

00:22:55.583 --> 00:22:57.794
Not too far from hunter's point?

00:23:01.384 --> 00:23:03.555
Same place where those
other murders happened.

00:23:03.558 --> 00:23:06.010
I'm telling you, it's the
werewolf's hunting grounds.

00:23:07.396 --> 00:23:09.457
But that doesn't mean it's
gonna be out there tonight.

00:23:09.460 --> 00:23:11.171
It's the right time of the lunar cycle.

00:23:11.935 --> 00:23:13.996
I know it's a long shot.

00:23:13.999 --> 00:23:15.088
You're forgetting something.

00:23:15.091 --> 00:23:16.431
Maddie's probably gonna turn soon.

00:23:16.434 --> 00:23:18.916
We can't let her take off
to an all-You-Can-Eat buffet.

00:23:19.831 --> 00:23:21.090
I'll stay with her.

00:23:21.093 --> 00:23:22.694
And if she busts loose?

00:23:24.540 --> 00:23:26.054
Sam? I'll do it.

00:23:26.564 --> 00:23:29.096
Sam. I'll shoot her, all right?

00:23:29.911 --> 00:23:32.082
But, dean, I need you to go out there.

00:23:32.125 --> 00:23:33.565
At least go look for the thing.

00:23:33.568 --> 00:23:34.768
Dean, please.

00:23:34.771 --> 00:23:36.531
We can save this girl.

00:23:40.312 --> 00:23:41.601
Fine.

00:23:48.799 --> 00:23:50.409
Please.

00:23:51.845 --> 00:23:53.736
Just let me go.

00:24:18.628 --> 00:24:19.808
Look...

00:24:21.404 --> 00:24:23.605
I know you're scared.

00:24:23.608 --> 00:24:26.872
I also know that there's no way
in hell you're gonna believe me.

00:24:28.057 --> 00:24:30.018
But I'm doing this...

00:24:30.983 --> 00:24:33.465
Because I'm trying to help you.

00:24:34.580 --> 00:24:35.783
I'm not gonna lie, all right?

00:24:35.786 --> 00:24:38.275
The odds aren't exactly in our favor.

00:24:38.768 --> 00:24:43.996
But if this goes the
way I pray it does...

00:24:44.540 --> 00:24:46.068
I'll untie you,

00:24:46.994 --> 00:24:50.609
And I'll walk out that door,
and I'll never come back.

00:24:51.774 --> 00:24:54.156
You'll live the rest of your life...

00:24:57.306 --> 00:25:00.809
And I'll just be a bad memory.

00:26:16.654 --> 00:26:17.372
Hey!

00:26:59.690 --> 00:27:01.250
It happened...

00:27:01.253 --> 00:27:02.933
Again.

00:27:03.758 --> 00:27:05.338
Where am I?

00:27:06.173 --> 00:27:08.324
H-Help me.

00:27:09.139 --> 00:27:11.490
God. Oh, my god.

00:27:11.493 --> 00:27:14.466
Easy gelen just take it easy

00:27:44.609 --> 00:27:46.300
It should be over now.

00:27:49.118 --> 00:27:51.250
You'll never see me again.

00:28:15.311 --> 00:28:17.151
It was sort of sad, actually.

00:28:17.565 --> 00:28:19.817
Glenn had no clue what was going on.

00:28:22.345 --> 00:28:25.468
Why do you think he turned Madison
instead of just killing her?

00:28:25.471 --> 00:28:26.781
I don't know.

00:28:26.784 --> 00:28:28.995
He kind of seemed to
have a thing for her.

00:28:28.998 --> 00:28:31.470
Maybe his primal instinct did, too.

00:28:32.515 --> 00:28:36.069
Maybe he was looking for a
little hot breeding action.

00:28:36.072 --> 00:28:37.783
Yeah. Something like that.

00:28:38.687 --> 00:28:39.977
So?

00:28:41.142 --> 00:28:42.121
So what?

00:28:42.124 --> 00:28:43.805
Speaking of madison... oh, whatever.

00:28:43.808 --> 00:28:46.771
You liked her. Maybe, uh
- Dean.

00:28:46.774 --> 00:28:48.850
She thought I was a
stark-Raving lunatic.

00:28:48.853 --> 00:28:49.612
You saved her life.

00:28:49.615 --> 00:28:51.570
But she doesn't know that.

00:28:52.535 --> 00:28:56.169
You know, for a stakeout,
your car's a bit conspicous.

00:28:56.487 --> 00:28:57.672
What are you still doing here?

00:28:57.675 --> 00:28:58.724
Honestly? Uh...

00:29:00.411 --> 00:29:02.478
We're pretty sure you're
not gonna turn tonight,

00:29:02.481 --> 00:29:04.909
But we got to be 100%,

00:29:04.912 --> 00:29:07.512
So, you know, we're... lurking.

00:29:09.549 --> 00:29:12.201
Look, I know this sounds crazy
- It sure does.

00:29:14.058 --> 00:29:16.259
Well, if we're gonna wait it out...

00:29:16.523 --> 00:29:18.774
We might as well do it together.

00:29:27.615 --> 00:29:29.836
You were telling the truth, weren't you?

00:29:29.839 --> 00:29:32.011
About everything.

00:29:33.968 --> 00:29:37.111
What you did -It was to help me.

00:29:37.715 --> 00:29:38.985
Yeah.

00:29:38.988 --> 00:29:41.440
I did all those horrible things...

00:29:42.705 --> 00:29:44.656
When I turned.

00:29:46.312 --> 00:29:47.893
You didn't know.

00:29:56.392 --> 00:29:59.015
So when will we know for sure?

00:29:59.018 --> 00:30:00.979
Moonrise?  No, I don't think so.

00:30:00.982 --> 00:30:02.191
You turned middle of
the night last night.

00:30:02.194 --> 00:30:04.506
I think we got to hang in until sunup.

00:30:12.044 --> 00:30:15.067
Well, looks like we got
ourselves a few hours to kill.

00:30:15.420 --> 00:30:17.031
Poker, anyone?

00:30:40.961 --> 00:30:42.271
Oh, no, you guys talk.

00:30:58.526 --> 00:31:00.848
Does -Does this mean it worked?

00:31:00.851 --> 00:31:02.552
Yeah, I think so.

00:31:04.328 --> 00:31:06.820
Oh, god, thank you.

00:31:06.823 --> 00:31:09.706
Thank you so much.

00:31:15.340 --> 00:31:17.541
You too, Dean.

00:31:17.544 --> 00:31:18.934
Thank you.

00:31:18.937 --> 00:31:20.848
Ah, don't mention it.

00:31:24.779 --> 00:31:33.012
So, I'm just gonna head back to the hotel
and watch some pay-Per-View or something.

00:31:40.540 --> 00:31:42.261
That was smooth.

00:31:43.075 --> 00:31:45.096
He means well.

00:31:45.099 --> 00:31:48.553
He means he thinks
you're gonna get laid.

00:31:50.059 --> 00:31:51.950
Look, I --
It's okay.

00:31:51.953 --> 00:31:53.112
No.

00:31:53.115 --> 00:31:55.477
I know I scared the crap
out of you, all right?

00:31:56.632 --> 00:31:58.233
I -I mean, I tied you to a chair.

00:31:58.236 --> 00:32:02.241
That's right up there with
me scratching up your face.

00:32:04.849 --> 00:32:07.000
There's just no way...

00:32:07.685 --> 00:32:09.846
We could go back, you know?

00:32:11.101 --> 00:32:12.962
To before it happened.

00:32:12.965 --> 00:32:14.185
You're right.

00:32:15.180 --> 00:32:17.461
There's just no way.

00:34:11.632 --> 00:34:13.583
She -She turned.

00:34:13.586 --> 00:34:14.575
What?

00:34:14.578 --> 00:34:16.759
I couldn't grab her in time.

00:34:17.153 --> 00:34:18.713
We'll find her, sammy.

00:34:18.716 --> 00:34:20.336
I already called bobby.

00:34:20.339 --> 00:34:23.954
He doesn't know anything, except he knew
severing the bloodline wouldn't work.

00:34:23.957 --> 00:34:26.378
They all say it's
impossible to reverse it.

00:34:26.381 --> 00:34:28.503
How come she didn't turn
when we were with her?

00:34:28.506 --> 00:34:30.197
You put her to bed and
then she wolfed out.

00:34:30.200 --> 00:34:31.519
Maybe she's got to be asleep to turn.

00:34:31.522 --> 00:34:32.881
What the hell does it matter?

00:34:32.884 --> 00:34:35.477
We got to find some way to
help her, some legend we missed.

00:34:35.480 --> 00:34:37.250
Don't you think someone
we know would have known?

00:34:37.253 --> 00:34:39.965
Then we have to look harder
until we find something.

00:34:40.309 --> 00:34:43.222
Sammy, I don't think we
got a choice here anymore.

00:34:44.678 --> 00:34:45.426
What?

00:34:45.429 --> 00:34:47.841
She's a sweet girl, but part of her is
- Evil?

00:34:47.844 --> 00:34:48.472
Yeah.

00:34:48.475 --> 00:34:50.306
That's what they say about me, dean.

00:34:50.309 --> 00:34:53.753
So me you won't kill, but her
you're just gonna blow away?

00:34:56.241 --> 00:34:57.511
Sam?

00:34:57.514 --> 00:34:58.963
Madison, where are you?

00:34:58.966 --> 00:35:01.549
I don't -I don't -I
don't know where I am.

00:35:01.932 --> 00:35:03.583
Do you see any street signs?

00:35:03.586 --> 00:35:05.797
Um... yeah, yeah.

00:35:05.800 --> 00:35:07.290
Middle point.

00:35:07.293 --> 00:35:08.182
Hold on, maddie.

00:35:08.185 --> 00:35:10.376
We're coming to get you.
Just stay where you are.

00:35:22.654 --> 00:35:25.647
I don't remember anything.

00:35:27.373 --> 00:35:30.166
I probably killed someone last night.

00:35:31.261 --> 00:35:32.701
Didn't I?

00:35:35.569 --> 00:35:37.400
There's no way to know yet.

00:35:37.403 --> 00:35:40.246
Is there something else we
can try to make it go away?

00:35:40.249 --> 00:35:41.478
We'll find something.

00:35:41.481 --> 00:35:44.504
There's got to be
some answer -Somewhere.

00:35:44.507 --> 00:35:46.238
That's not entirely true.

00:35:46.241 --> 00:35:48.242
Madison, you deserve to know.

00:35:49.407 --> 00:35:51.619
We've scoured every source.

00:35:52.333 --> 00:35:54.093
There's just no cure.

00:35:56.421 --> 00:35:58.111
Is -Is he right?

00:36:11.521 --> 00:36:14.474
Well, we could lock
you up at night, but...

00:36:14.477 --> 00:36:16.999
You bust out, and some night you will...

00:36:17.914 --> 00:36:19.865
Someone else dies.

00:36:23.545 --> 00:36:25.917
I'm sorry. I am.

00:36:34.116 --> 00:36:37.290
So I guess that's all
there is to it, then.

00:36:38.505 --> 00:36:40.316
Stop it. Don't talk like that.

00:36:40.319 --> 00:36:42.530
Sam, I don't want to hurt anyone else.

00:36:42.533 --> 00:36:44.584
I don't want to hurt you.

00:36:52.102 --> 00:36:53.512
Put that down.

00:36:53.515 --> 00:36:55.847
I can't do it myself.

00:36:58.595 --> 00:37:01.789
I need you to help me.  Madison, no.

00:37:01.792 --> 00:37:02.801
Sam.

00:37:03.084 --> 00:37:06.047
I'm a monster. You don't have to be.

00:37:06.812 --> 00:37:09.384
We could find a way, all right?

00:37:09.387 --> 00:37:11.388
I can. I'm gonna save you.

00:37:11.391 --> 00:37:12.981
You tried.

00:37:12.984 --> 00:37:14.845
I know you tried.

00:37:15.198 --> 00:37:17.831
This is all there is left.

00:37:18.264 --> 00:37:19.995
Help me, sam.

00:37:21.150 --> 00:37:23.332
I want you to do it.

00:37:24.467 --> 00:37:26.768
I want it to be you. I can't.

00:37:26.771 --> 00:37:29.043
I don't want to die.

00:37:29.046 --> 00:37:30.806
I don't.

00:37:31.321 --> 00:37:34.003
But I can't live like this.

00:37:36.090 --> 00:37:38.772
This is the way you can save me.

00:37:40.399 --> 00:37:42.570
Please.

00:37:44.046 --> 00:37:47.039
I'm asking you to save me.

00:38:42.152 --> 00:38:43.732
Sam

00:38:52.452 --> 00:38:53.512
I'm sorry.

00:38:53.515 --> 00:38:55.095
No, you're right.

00:38:56.400 --> 00:38:58.642
She's right.

00:38:59.927 --> 00:39:01.708
Sammy, I got this one. I'll do it.

00:39:01.711 --> 00:39:03.732
She asked me to.

00:39:04.707 --> 00:39:07.770
You don't have to. Yes, I do.

00:39:12.793 --> 00:39:14.654
Please.

00:39:24.015 --> 00:39:26.257
Just wait here.

00:00:07.081 --> 00:00:08.584
